WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:05.967
Bill Sikes dragged Oliver through the narrow streets so quickly that Nancy had trouble keeping up.

2
00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:12.118
"Grab hold of her hand," Sikes said roughly to Oliver. "And don't you dare make a sound."

3
00:00:12.119 --> 00:00:15.943
They were in a dark corner, out of view of any passersby.

4
00:00:15.944 --> 00:00:22.872
Oliver realized there was no point in resisting. He held out his hand, which Nancy clasped tightly.

5
00:00:22.873 --> 00:00:30.016
"Give me the other hand," said Sikes. "Here, Bull's-eye!" he called to the white dog.

6
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.351
The dog looked up and growled.

7
00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:39.516
"See here, dog. If this boy cries out, grab him and hold on tight. Do you understand?"

8
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:43.016
The dog looked menacingly at Oliver and growled again.

9
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:49.231
They set off again into the dark night. The lights in the shops were dim through the heavy mist.

10
00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:54.318
Bill was dragging Oliver past the prison when a church bell struck the hour.

11
00:00:54.319 --> 00:00:58.258
"I wonder whether the prisoners can hear that," said Nancy.

12
00:00:58.259 --> 00:01:06.163
"Of course they can," replied Sikes. "The last time I was locked up for housebreaking, I could hear every sound at night."

13
00:01:06.164 --> 00:01:10.322
"Poor fellows," said Nancy, who was still looking at the prison.

14
00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:17.155
But there wasn't time to think about prisoners. Sikes yanked on Oliver's wrist, and Nancy came along too.

15
00:01:17.156 --> 00:01:20.497
They walked through deserted streets for half an hour.

16
00:01:20.498 --> 00:01:26.000
At last they stopped in front of a run-down house with an ancient "For Rent" sign on the door.

17
00:01:26.024 --> 00:01:28.148
Nancy rang the bell.

18
00:01:28.148 --> 00:01:36.544
Then they crossed the street and stood under a streetlamp so someone inside could see who they were. At last the door softly opened.

19
00:01:36.545 --> 00:01:41.851
Sikes seized a terrified Oliver by the collar, and they went quickly inside the house.

20
00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:44.878
The hallway was very dark.

21
00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:52.792
They waited while the person who had let them in barred the door. Then he lit a candle. It was the Artful Dodger.

22
00:01:52.793 --> 00:01:55.878
He grinned at Oliver but didn't say anything.

23
00:01:55.902 --> 00:01:59.198
He led them downstairs and through an empty kitchen.

24
00:01:59.198 --> 00:02:04.864
When he opened the door to a low room, they were greeted with shouts of laughter from Charley Bates.

25
00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:14.927
"Oh, my goodness!" cried Charley. "Here he is! Look at him, Fagin! Hold me, somebody, or I'll die laughing."

26
00:02:14.928 --> 00:02:19.432
At this, Charley fell on the floor and rolled around and laughed some more.

27
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:25.011
Then he jumped up and held the candle so close to Oliver's new jacket that it nearly caught fire.

28
00:02:25.012 --> 00:02:35.186
"Look at his clothes, Fagin! Superfine cloth and a stylish cut! And his books too. He's such a gentleman now."

29
00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:41.757
"Delighted to see you looking so well," Fagin said to Oliver with mock humility.

30
00:02:41.758 --> 00:02:48.424
"Why didn't you write, my dear, and say you were coming? We'd have warmed something up for supper."

31
00:02:48.425 --> 00:02:55.154
Oliver was too shaken to respond. He didn't even react when the Dodger started going through his pockets.

32
00:02:55.155 --> 00:03:00.797
"What's this?" cried the Dodger, holding up the five-pound note that Mr. Brownlow had given Oliver.

33
00:03:00.798 --> 00:03:05.043
"That's mine, Fagin," said Sikes as Fagin seized the note.

34
00:03:05.044 --> 00:03:10.480
"No, it's mine," said Fagin. "You shall have the books, Bill."

35
00:03:10.481 --> 00:03:18.139
"Hand it over," said Sikes. "Do you think Nancy and I have nothing to do but kidnap every boy that escapes from you?

36
00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.790
If you don't give me that money, I'll take the boy back again."

37
00:03:21.791 --> 00:03:27.956
Fagin started in surprise. Oliver started too, but for a different reason.

38
00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:33.107
He hoped that their dispute might really result in his being taken back to Mr. Brownlow.

39
00:03:33.108 --> 00:03:42.115
Sikes plucked the note from Fagin's hand. Looking the old man coolly in the face, Sikes folded up the note and tied it in his neckerchief.

40
00:03:42.116 --> 00:03:48.845
"That's for our share of the trouble," he said. "Keep the books and sell them if you're not fond of reading."

41
00:03:48.846 --> 00:03:55.448
"They're very pretty," said Charley, pretending to read one. "Beautiful writing, isn't it, Oliver?"

42
00:03:55.449 --> 00:04:00.186
"They belong to the kind gentleman who took care of me," said Oliver in distress.

43
00:04:00.187 --> 00:04:09.512
"I would have died from the fever if it weren't for him and the housekeeper. Oh, please send back the books and the money. The gentleman will think I stole them."

44
00:04:09.513 --> 00:04:14.568
With these pleading words, Oliver fell on his knees in front of Fagin.

45
00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:22.822
"You're right, Oliver." Fagin looked around at the others in the room. "This couldn't have happened better if we'd planned it."

46
00:04:22.823 --> 00:04:32.885
"But they won't go looking for him," said Sikes. "They're soft-hearted people. They know if he's found, they'll have to bring charges and he'll get sent to prison."

47
00:04:32.886 --> 00:04:42.823
Oliver looked from one person to the other. Suddenly he jumped to his feet and tore wildly from the room, uttering shrieks for help that made the old house echo.

48
00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:53.649
"Don't let the dog go after him, Bill." Nancy sprang to the door and closed it as Fagin, the Dodger, and Charley ran after Oliver. "The dog will tear him to pieces."

49
00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:59.474
"That would serve him right." Sikes grabbed Nancy's wrists and they began to struggle.

50
00:04:59.475 --> 00:05:04.292
"What's the matter here?" cried Fagin as he and the boys returned with Oliver.

51
00:05:04.293 --> 00:05:08.117
"The girl's gone mad," said Sikes.

52
00:05:08.118 --> 00:05:11.451
"No, she hasn't," retorted Nancy.

53
00:05:11.452 --> 00:05:20.872
Fagin turned his attention to Oliver. "So you wanted to get away from me, my dear? Wanted to call the police for assistance?"

54
00:05:20.873 --> 00:05:26.522
He picked up a club lying near the fireplace. "We'll cure you of that."

55
00:05:26.523 --> 00:05:30.118
Nancy rushed forward and flung the club into the fire.

56
00:05:30.119 --> 00:05:40.113
"I won't stand by and let you hurt him," she shouted. "He's a thief, a liar, and all that's bad from this night forward. Isn't that enough?"

57
00:05:40.114 --> 00:05:43.700
"You're a fine one to talk," said Sikes.

58
00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:51.764
"I know I am." Nancy turned her anger on Fagin. "I've thieved for you ever since I was half as old as Oliver.

59
00:05:51.765 --> 00:05:57.597
I know what kind of life you're leading him into. You're the wretch who ruined my life."

60
00:05:57.598 --> 00:06:05.836
And with that, she rushed at Fagin. She probably would have pummeled him with her fists if Sikes hadn't grabbed her and held her back.

61
00:06:05.837 --> 00:06:09.082
Nancy struggled for a moment and then fainted.

62
00:06:09.083 --> 00:06:15.169
Fagin wiped his forehead and smiled at Oliver. "Charley, show Oliver to bed."

63
00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:19.336
"He shouldn't wear his best clothes tomorrow, should he?" asked Charley.

64
00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:22.478
"Certainly not," Fagin replied.

65
00:06:22.479 --> 00:06:27.566
Charley led Oliver into the kitchen where there were several sacks on the floor for beds.

66
00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:32.733
And here Charley produced the old clothes that Oliver had given to Mr. Brownlow's servant.

67
00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:40.542
"Fagin knows everyone who's got clothes for sale," explained Charley. "He came upon yours and knew you'd want them back."

68
00:06:40.543 --> 00:06:44.296
Oliver took off his new clothes and handed them to Charley.

69
00:06:44.297 --> 00:06:54.849
"What fun this is!" said Charley. Then he departed from the room, leaving Oliver in the dark and locking the door behind him.

